    <p class="tiny">
      The heartbeat takes file:, serial:, tcp: or none. Field never listens for connections: every tcp: endpoint
      connects out. Spec section 8.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-top: 16px">
      <strong>Checkpoint identity.</strong> The keys that decide results are <code>task</code>, <code>adapter</code>,{' '}
      <code>input</code>, <code>output</code>, <code>policy</code>, <code>replicas</code>, <code>strikes</code>,{' '}
      <code>window</code>, <code>kat_every</code>, <code>record_max</code>, <code>state_max</code>, the known-answer
      records and the fault schedule by content, <code>oracle</code>, and <code>input_backlog</code> when it is{' '}
      <code>newest</code>. Change one and Field refuses the old checkpoint with exit 2 and does not overwrite it; move
      it away to start fresh. The other keys only tune a run and can change between restarts. <code>candidate</code> is
      not in the identity: a staged update comes in on the running run.
    </p>

